# Line endings
# ------------
# The cluster is Linux, the dev box is Windows. Without this, whichever machine
# last wrote a file decides its endings and git records the flip as every line
# changed - a one-line edit lands as a 1,181-line diff, and a real change hides
# inside it. Worse for *.job and *.sh: a CRLF shebang makes Linux fail the whole
# job with "bad interpreter: /bin/bash^M".
#
# text=auto lets git classify text vs binary per file; eol=lf pins the
# working-tree copy to LF on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicit for anything the pipeline writes or that must never be rewritten.
# text=auto sniffs for NUL bytes near the start of a file and can misclassify
# one that has none - which is how a .png ended up looking like a CRLF text file
# when this repo was surveyed.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.zip   binary
*.pkl   binary
*.faiss binary
*.npy   binary
*.npz   binary
